# Video and audio stay out of git. Copy, renderers, checkers and the static
# post images go in.
#
# This file DOES NOT introduce a policy. It writes down the one already chosen
# in 833ca45, "commit the working tree, and stop 551 MB of renders from
# entering a public repo", so the next session does not have to re-derive it
# from what happens to be tracked.
#
# Measured 2026-08-01, package is 330 MB on disk:
#
#   tracked    20 MB   144 png + 9 ttf + about 2.6 MB of md, py, txt, json
#   ignored   325 MB   mp4 and wav
#
# WHY THE LINE SITS THERE
#
#   The static images ARE the deliverable. They are what gets attached to a
#   post, they are small, and they are reproducible from the _build renderers
#   which are themselves tracked. Keeping them tracked means a logo change is
#   reviewable as a diff of what shipped.
#
#   Video and audio are 325 MB of the 330. Git history is permanent, so a
#   blob is in every clone forever even after a later delete, and neither
#   diffs nor reviews. THIS REPO IS PUBLIC (github.com/Tenerife365/GetBrandGeo,
#   confirmed 2026-08-01), so committing the cuts would also publish the
#   campaign before it is posted.
#
# A .gitignore DOES NOT UNTRACK anything already committed. The 144 png stay
# tracked and their future edits keep showing in git status, which is the
# intended behaviour, not an oversight.
#
# THE VIDEO HAS NO BACKUP HERE and never did, since the package was untracked
# from creation on 2026-07-30 until 833ca45. Nothing is lost by this file, but
# the masters need somewhere built for binaries.

*.mp4
*.mov
*.mkv
*.webm
*.wav
*.mp3
*.m4a
*.aac

# Build junk, never wanted
__pycache__/
*.pyc
